{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"resume","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Resuming an interrupted evaluation fails when its saved request includes the retired model, preventing supported work from continuing."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A valid bare IPv6 SSH destination causes every remote-management action to throw before contacting the host."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An SSH alias that differs from the provider endpoint prevents credential lookup and provider enablement updates, yielding an incorrect health result."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Persisted routing settings naming a retired model or provider cause factory construction to fail after upgrade."},{"id":"C7","consequence":"diag","trigger":"normal","reason":"The documented link lands on the wrong provider section instead of the promised LAN example."},{"id":"C8","consequence":"outage","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Following the stale binary location without an override can produce a service unit that cannot start the remote server."},{"id":"C1b","consequence":"resume","trigger":"plausible","reason":"A saved fallback chain containing the retired model prevents an interrupted evaluation from resuming even when supported targets remain."}]}